---
/**
 * Progress, recorded on paper.
 *
 * A tick box per session and per unit, one sheet per child. The sheets are
 * generated from the course itself, so a unit built later gets a sheet with no
 * work here — and the syllabus check on each sheet is the unit's own can-do
 * list, which is what decides whether to move on.
 */
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Steps from "../../components/Steps.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
import TickSheet from "../../components/TickSheet.astro";
import PageNav from "../../components/PageNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import stage1 from "../../data/stage1.json";

const units = (await getCollection("units")).sort((a, b) => a.data.number - b.data.number);
const sessions = await getCollection("sessions");

const sheets = units
  .map((u) => ({
    number: u.data.number,
    title: u.data.title,
    canDos: u.data.canDos,
    sessions: sessions
      .filter((s) => s.data.unit === u.data.number)
      .sort((a, b) => a.data.number - b.data.number)
      .map((s) => ({ number: s.data.number, title: s.data.title, minutes: s.data.minutes })),
  }))
  .filter((s) => s.sessions.length > 0);

const waiting = stage1.filter((u) => !sheets.some((s) => s.number === u.number));
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---
<Base
  title="Progress — Italian GCSE"
  eyebrow="Pearson Edexcel GCSE Italian · 1IN0"
  heading="Keeping the record"
  standfirst="One sheet per child per unit, ticked by hand. Two lists: the sessions worked through, and the can-dos that decide whether to move on."
  description="Printable tick sheets for recording progress through a home-taught Edexcel GCSE Italian course: one per child per unit, sessions and can-do checks."
>
  <Breadcrumbs slot="nav" trail={[
    { label: "Contents", href: `${base}/` },
    { label: "Progress" },
  ]} />

  <Section kicker="How it works">Paper, on purpose</Section>

  <p>Nothing is stored on this site. There is no account and no name anywhere on
  it — the record lives on a printed sheet in the front of the notebook, where
  whoever is teaching can see it without opening anything.</p>

  <p>That also keeps the record honest. A tick means someone watched it happen.</p>

  <Section kicker="The routine">How to record it</Section>

  <Steps>
    <li><strong>Print one sheet per child, per unit</strong> — the sheets are below, one to a page. Write the child's name at the top.</li>
    <li><strong>Tick a session on the day you do it</strong>, and put the date beside it. A session is done when it has been worked through once, aloud, from beginning to end. Not when it is perfect.</li>
    <li><strong>Leave the can-dos alone until the unit is finished.</strong> They are not a summary of the sessions; they are a separate check, and ticking them as you go defeats them.</li>
    <li><strong>At the end of the unit, test each can-do once</strong> — cold, with no reminders, on a different day from the last session. Tick only the ones that are true without prompting, and date them.</li>
    <li><strong>Move on when every can-do is ticked.</strong> If one is not, go back to the session that taught it and do that session again. Repeating one session is normal; carrying an untrue can-do into the next unit is not.</li>
  </Steps>

  <Note lead="What is deliberately not recorded">
    <p>No marks, no scores, no minutes spent. A nine-year-old's progress through
    the sound system is not a percentage, and a number here would be invented.
    The can-dos are the assessment: each one is either true or it is not, and
    the ones on these sheets are the statements the specification actually turns
    on.</p>
  </Note>

  <Note lead="One sheet each" child>
    <p>If you are teaching more than one child, print a sheet each and keep them
    apart. They will not move at the same speed, and a shared sheet turns the
    slower one's record into a comparison with the faster one every time it is
    opened. Same course, separate paper.</p>
  </Note>

  <Section kicker="The sheets">One per unit</Section>

  <p class="noprint">Print this page for every sheet at once, or print a single
  page from the browser's print dialogue. Each unit starts a new page.</p>

  {sheets.map((s) => (
    <TickSheet number={s.number} title={s.title} sessions={s.sessions} canDos={s.canDos} />
  ))}

  {waiting.length > 0 && (
    <p class="noprint waiting">
      {`Sheets for ${waiting.length} more unit${waiting.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} appear here as they are built — Unit ${String(waiting[0].number).padStart(2, "0")} onwards. There is nothing to record until there is something to teach.`}
    </p>
  )}

  <PageNav
    prev={{ kicker: "Back to", label: "Contents", href: `${base}/` }}
    next={sheets[0] && {
      kicker: `Unit ${String(sheets[0].number).padStart(2, "0")}`,
      label: sheets[0].title,
      href: `${base}/units/${sheets[0].number}/`,
    }}
  />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" left="Edexcel GCSE Italian 1IN0 · Progress" />
</Base>

<style>
  .waiting {
    font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--ink-faint);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 1rem; max-width: 44rem;
  }
</style>
